  "tagline": "200-byte browser key-value store that persists data in the page's history.state.",
  "description": "Histore is a tiny JavaScript library by Jason Miller (developit) that turns the browser's navigation state into a key-value store. Values are written with history.replaceState, so they survive reloads of the same tab and back/forward navigation but, unlike localStorage or sessionStorage, are not shared with other tabs. Objects are cloned with the structured clone algorithm, and the README cites room for about 640 KB of data. The whole library is about 200 bytes and exposes only get and set. It shipped as 1.0.0 in May 2018 and has not changed since. It is a neat trick for per-tab UI state, not a database for application data.",
